@startuml
' issue #2622: CSS "Padding" has no effect on the cells of a Creole table
' (here rendered inside a note), unlike "skinparam padding" - the legacy
' table renderer (StripeTable) reads ISkinParam.getPadding() directly and
' never consults the style/CSS engine. This currently renders identically
' to the same table with no style at all - pinning that gap so a fix
' shows up as an intentional diff here.
<style>
element {
  Padding: 20
}
</style>
(*) --> "test"
note left
|= H1 |= H2 |
| a | b |
end note
@enduml
